# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0). GitHub reads this file and shows a
# "Cite this repository" button with APA and BibTeX entries. Validate changes with
# `pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate`.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, data or analysis, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Brewery Portfolio Development: geographic analysis, spatial clustering and location prediction for Open Brewery DB"
authors:
  - family-names: Waisi
    given-names: Hedyeh
    email: waisihedyeh@gmail.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
repository-code: "https://github.com/hedyehwaisi/Brewery-Portfolio-Development"
url: "https://brewery-dashboard.onrender.com/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - breweries
  - open-brewery-db
  - geographic-analysis
  - spatial-clustering
  - dbscan
  - hdbscan
  - optics
  - kernel-density-estimation
  - streamlit
  - plotly
  - data-quality
abstract: >-
  A reproducible analysis of an Open Brewery DB snapshot (11,959 brewery records): data quality
  and duplicate checks, coordinate corrections, geographic distribution across countries, states
  and cities, density-based spatial clustering (DBSCAN, HDBSCAN, OPTICS) with full parameter
  grids, and a probability model for where the next brewery is likely to open. Results are stored
  in SQLite and presented in a multi-page Streamlit dashboard. Code is MIT licensed; text and
  figures are CC BY 4.0; bundled data keeps the terms of Open Brewery DB (MIT), GeoNames
  (CC BY 4.0) and OpenStreetMap (ODbL).
references:
  - type: database
    title: "Open Brewery DB"
    authors:
      - name: "Open Brewery DB"
    url: "https://www.openbrewerydb.org/"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/openbrewerydb/openbrewerydb"
    license: MIT
    notes: "Brewery records fetched from the public API."
  - type: database
    title: "GeoNames geographical database"
    authors:
      - name: "GeoNames"
    url: "https://www.geonames.org"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    notes: "Capitals and city center points (cities500, admin1CodesASCII, admin2Codes, countryInfo)."
  - type: database
    title: "OpenStreetMap"
    authors:
      - name: "OpenStreetMap contributors"
    url: "https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"
    license: ODbL-1.0
    notes: "Nominatim geocoding for 68 city centers and reverse-geocoded evidence; basemap tiles."
